<article class="env-lemma" id="0934">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0934">Lemma <span data-tag="0934">18.30.1</span>.</a> Let $(\mathcal{C}, \mathcal{O})$ be a ringed site. Let $\{ U_ i \to U\} $ be a covering of $\mathcal{C}$. Then the sequence </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  \bigoplus j_{U_ i \times _ U U_ j!}\mathcal{O}_{U_ i \times _ U U_ j} \to \bigoplus j_{U_ i!}\mathcal{O}_{U_ i} \to j_!\mathcal{O}_ U \to 0  \]
</div>
  <p> is exact. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      For any $\mathcal{O}$-module $\mathcal{F}$ the functor $\mathop{\mathrm{Hom}}\nolimits _\mathcal {O}(-, \mathcal{F})$ turns our sequence into the exact sequence $0 \to \mathcal{F}(U) \to \prod \mathcal{F}(U_ i) \to \prod \mathcal{F}(U_ i \times _ U U_ j)$, see (<a href="/tag/0G1V" data-tag="0G1V">18.19.2.1</a>). The lemma follows from this and Homology, Lemma <a href="/tag/05AA" data-tag="05AA">12.5.8</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>